{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100}, "sp": "fc", "rep": 217, "hyps": [{"edit_param": "learning_rate_init", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "low", "direction": "higher", "why": "Raising a very small learning rate fixes undertraining within 243 epochs, while raising an already large one does not."}, {"edit_param": "learning_rate_init", "edit_dir": "down", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "higher", "why": "Cutting an overly large learning rate restores stable training, giving large gains (e.g. experiments 69, 77, 78)."}, {"edit_param": "depth", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "lower", "why": "Deeper networks at a large learning rate diverge more easily (experiments 47, 57, 58 show huge drops)."}, {"edit_param": "alpha", "edit_dir": "down", "cond_param": "alpha", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "higher", "why": "Strong L2 penalty underfits, so weakening it helps (experiments 6, 7)."}, {"edit_param": "alpha", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "alpha", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "lower", "why": "Pushing an already strong L2 penalty higher causes underfitting (experiment 14)."}, {"edit_param": "batch_size", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "higher", "why": "Larger batches give less noisy gradients, which stabilizes training at large learning rates (experiments 23, 25, 27)."}, {"edit_param": "width", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "width", "cond_band": "low", "direction": "higher", "why": "Narrow networks are capacity-limited, so widening them helps more than widening already wide ones."}, {"edit_param": "learning_rate_init", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "lower", "why": "Increasing an already large learning rate causes instability (experiments 67, 73, 74)."}, {"edit_param": "depth", "edit_dir": "down", "cond_param": "learning_rate_